GPL-3.0-or-later code is kept behind the bridge headers
`runner/src/gpu3d.h` and `runner/src/wifi.h` and, for the native DS render
sinks, inside `render/src/ds/` and its build-time shader generator
`tools/ds_shader_gen.cpp`. The 3D sink implements melonDS's `Renderer3D` and
links the vendored `GPU3D_Texcache` and `xxhash` rather than reimplementing the
texture cache: that code is already the device model's texture path, and a
second copy would duplicate GPL-derived behaviour instead of isolating it. The
runtime sink stays behind `ds_3d.h`, the C ABI in `runner_bridge.cpp`, and
`GPU3D::SetCurrentRenderer`.

The shader generator includes the vendored melonDS `GPU3D_Compute_shaders.h`,
emits the Vulkan GLSL variants at build time, and those variants are compiled to
SPIR-V and embedded in `pkmn_render_ds`. The generated shader source and
embedded SPIR-V are GPL-3.0-or-later, like the melonDS source they are derived
from; neither is committed to this repository. The generator is build-only and
is not part of the runtime boundary.

See `docs/adr/0007-native-ds-render-sinks.md` and the GPLv3 §5(a) notices in
`patches/ndsrecomp/`. Per-module license attribution in upstream
`THIRD_PARTY_ATTRIBUTION.md` applies.

The pinned `ndsrecomp` tree carries local, tracked modifications of our own
(`patches/ndsrecomp/`, applied at configure time when the runner is built and
inert otherwise): a guarded present hook in `runner/src/frontend.cpp` (`0001`);
a guarded native DS render sink hook, the capture probe in `gpu2d.cpp`, and the
even-width parser in `frontend.cpp`, `main.cpp`, and `frontend_config.cpp`
(`0003`, applied on top of `0001`); a guarded GPU3D device accessor in
`runner/src/gpu3d.{h,cpp}` (`0004`); and a libslirp MSVC/POSIX portability fix
(`0002`). Their GPLv3 §5(a) change notices are in the files and patches. They
add only our own code, except the portability fix, and change no upstream
behaviour when the opt-in guards are off.
